gallery-collab: Changes from the Base Plugin
=============================================

This file tracks how this fork differs from the upstream gallery plugin
(https://github.com/splitbrain/dokuwiki-plugin-gallery). The original README
is kept unchanged; add an entry here whenever we extend or modify the code.

Base
----

  Upstream project : splitbrain/dokuwiki-plugin-gallery
  Base version     : 2026-09-02 (plugin.info.txt)
  Base commit      : ddde5b9 (master, "Merge pull request #219 ...")


Identity
--------

  Plugin name (base) : gallerycollab   (was: gallery) - install in lib/plugins/gallerycollab/
  Author             : Bruce DuPlanty <bduplanty@gmail.com>; original gallery plugin by Andreas Gohr
                       and contributors (credits and GPL 2 license kept in the source files)
  Renamed            : PHP namespace dokuwiki\plugin\gallerycollab, plugin classes
                       syntax_/action_plugin_gallerycollab_*, plugin_load() names, JS language/info keys
                       (LANG.plugins.gallerycollab, JSINFO.plugins.gallerycollab), AJAX call names, tests.
  Unchanged          : wiki syntax {{gallery>...}} and <gallery>, CSS classes (plugin-gallery,
                       gallery-*), the ProseMirror node name, the data/gallery-collab sidecar folder.
  plugin.info.txt url: still points at the upstream docs page - replace with this fork's URL.


Summary of differences
----------------------

  Collaborative captions: users in contributor groups suggest titles/captions, users in reviewer
  groups (and superusers) approve them. Approved captions override the image's own metadata when a
  gallery is rendered; originals are never lost (sidecar history, optional IPTC write-back for JPEG).
  Feed galleries are not supported.


Change log
----------

Add one entry per change, newest first, using this template:

  ### YYYY-MM-DD - Short title
  Files   : path/to/file.php, ...
  Purpose : why the change was made
  Details : what changed relative to the base behaviour
  Compat  : any syntax, config, or upstream-merge implications

  ### 2026-10-25 - Search and sort toolbar
  Files   : classes/Options.php, classes/XHTMLFormatter.php, script/toolbar.js, script.js, screen.less,
            conf/metadata.php, lang/en/lang.php, action/prosemirror.php, GalleryNode.php,
            script/prosemirror.js, _test/ToolbarTest.php
  Purpose : let visitors find images and reorder a gallery without reloading the page
  Details : - New boolean option "toolbar" (off by default): {{gallery>ns?toolbar}} or
              <gallery toolbar>; "notoolbar" turns it off; it can also be a default in the
              plugin's "options" setting and is a checkbox in the ProseMirror dialog.
            - Search field: space separated terms, all must match (title, caption, file name);
              case and accent insensitive; Esc clears it.
            - Sort selector: default order, title, date, file name (natural number order, so
              img_2 comes before img_10) plus an ascending/descending selector. "Date" is the
              image's own date, else the file's modification date; images without a date always
              come last.
            - Works across all pages of a paginated gallery: the browser rebuilds the pages from
              the filtered, sorted list. Shows "Showing N of M" and a no-match message.
            - Lightbox next/previous follows the filtered, sorted order (SimpleLightbox refresh()).
            - Server side: toolbar markup and per-figure data-title/-filename/-date/-search
              attributes (only when the option is on). The toolbar is hidden until JavaScript runs.
            - Titles and captions come from the approved captions, so searches match reviewed text.
            - The visitor's sort field and direction are remembered per gallery (page + gallery ID)
              in the browser's localStorage and restored on the next visit. The search text is not
              remembered. Unknown or damaged saved values and blocked storage are ignored; choosing
              the default order forgets the saved choice.
  Compat  : No change for galleries without the option. Wording is English only; other
            languages fall back to English until lang/*/lang.php entries are added.

  ### 2026-10-24 - Archive export tool and backup guide
  Files   : tools/export_captions.py, tools/test_export_captions.py, docs/BACKUP_AND_ARCHIVE.md
  Purpose : long-term archive of the latest approved titles/captions, independent of the wiki, for
            images whose file is not updated (non-JPEG, or write_iptc off)
  Details : Python 3.8+, standard library only. Runs locally against a downloaded data/media and
            data/gallery-collab. Writes titlesandcaptions/<namespace>/<image>.md for every image,
            index.html (browser view with filter) and index.json (for scripts). Never modifies inputs.
  Compat  : stand-alone, not loaded by DokuWiki. The tools/ and docs/ folders are ignored by the plugin.

  ### 2026-10-24 - Fix sidecar location with relative savedir
  Files   : classes/CaptionStore.php
  Purpose : with $conf['savedir'] = './data' the AJAX endpoint (lib/exe/) and doku.php used different
            folders, so approved captions never showed in galleries
  Details : CaptionStore::baseDir() anchors savedir at DOKU_INC
  Compat  : sidecar files already written by the old code sit in <wiki>/lib/exe/data/gallery-collab/;
            move that folder to <wiki>/data/gallery-collab/ (or re-approve the captions)

  ### 2026-10-24 - Gallery no longer re-enables page caching
  Files   : syntax/main.php
  Purpose : ~~NOCACHE~~ on a page was overridden because the gallery set info['cache'] = true
  Details : the gallery now only sets info['cache'] = false when the cache option is off
  Compat  : galleries on pages with ~~NOCACHE~~ are no longer cached (intended)

  ### 2026-10-24 - Rename plugin to gallerycollab
  Files   : plugin.info.txt, all PHP/JS under action/, syntax/, classes/, script/, _test/, conf/, README
  Purpose : make the fork installable next to / instead of the upstream gallery plugin
  Details : see "Identity" above. Config is now stored under plugin»gallerycollab»*, so settings
            from the old gallery plugin must be re-entered. Translations in lang/ need no change.
  Compat  : Existing pages keep working (same syntax). DokuWiki autoloading requires the folder to be
            named gallerycollab. Do not run this and the upstream gallery plugin together: both
            claim {{gallery>}}.

  ### 2026-10-24 - Collaborative captions (suggest / review)
  Files   : action/collab.php, classes/CaptionStore.php, script/collab.js, script.js, screen.less,
            classes/Image.php, classes/ListGallery.php, classes/XHTMLFormatter.php,
            conf/default.php, conf/metadata.php, lang/en/lang.php, lang/en/settings.php,
            _test/CaptionStoreTest.php
  Purpose : let a defined group suggest title/caption text for images without touching the file's
            EXIF/IPTC data, and let a reviewer group approve or edit what is displayed.
  Details : - New config: contributor_groups (default "user"), reviewer_groups (default "reviewer"),
              write_iptc (default off). Superusers are always reviewers.
            - Suggestions and approved overrides are stored per image as JSON in
              data/gallery-collab/<media id>.json (suggestions, override, history).
            - Image applies the override on load; list-gallery inline titles do not replace it.
            - AJAX endpoint ajax.php?call=gallery_collab (POST + sectok): get, suggest, approve,
              reject, delete, revert. Contributors see only their own suggestions.
            - A pencil button on each local thumbnail (shown to permitted users only) opens a dialog.
            - XHTML figures carry data-id (local images only).
            - Approving/reverting touches data/gallery-collab/.stamp; all rendered pages (xhtml cache)
              depend on it (PARSER_CACHE_USE) so cached output is refreshed.
            - Thumbnails show a badge (upper left) with the pending count: reviewers see all pending
              suggestions, contributors their own. Loaded via AJAX op "pending" because the page
              HTML is cached and identical for everyone; refreshed when the dialog closes.
            - With write_iptc and a writable JPEG plus upload ACL, Iptc.Headline / Iptc.Caption are
              also written. The sidecar override stays the source of truth.
  Compat  : No syntax change. Feed galleries and external images are unaffected.
            NOT YET RUN: no PHP/DokuWiki in the dev environment - tests and UI need a first run.


Upstream merge notes
--------------------

Record files with heavy local modifications here so future merges from
upstream can be handled carefully.

  classes/Image.php (constructor + applyOverride), classes/ListGallery.php, classes/XHTMLFormatter.php
  (data-id) and script.js (one include line) are small edits to upstream files. Everything else
  collab-related is in new files.
